# PrintDesk API: sample requests (REST Client extension for VS Code)
#
# START HERE:
#   1. Send "listOrders" first (below). Other requests read ids from its response.
#   2. Then send "createOrder". The get / update / status / delete requests use the
#      order it creates, so the seeded data is never touched.
#   3. Work top to bottom. After reloading VS Code, send both again.
#
# Local: leave @baseUrl as is. Live: swap it for the deployed URL.
# Local only: run `npm run seed` first so there is data to read.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

###
# ---------- SETUP (send these first) ----------

### Health check (also wakes a sleeping free-tier server) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### listOrders -> 200 (newest first; provides a customerId for later requests)
# @name listOrders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?limit=1

###
# ---------- HAPPY PATHS ----------

### List orders with filters, sorting and paging -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=printing&sort=dueDate&page=1&limit=5

### createOrder -> 201 (note the Location header and status "received")
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].customerId}}",
  "dueDate": "2030-01-15",
  "notes": "Sample order from orders.http"
}

### Get the order just created -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Update its details -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dueDate": "2030-02-01",
  "notes": "Due date moved back by customer"
}

### Change its status -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "printing"
}

### Filter by that status -> 200 (the order should appear)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=printing

### Delete the order just created -> 200
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

###
# ---------- FAILURE CASES ----------

### Order that no longer exists (deleted above) -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Valid id that does not exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/000000000000000000000000

### Malformed id -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/not-a-real-id

### Missing required customerId -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "no customer"
}

### customerId that matches no customer -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "000000000000000000000000"
}

### Unknown field -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].customerId}}",
  "priority": "high"
}

### Due date in the past -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].customerId}}",
  "dueDate": "2020-01-01"
}

### Invalid status value -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "shipped"
}

### Status cannot be changed through the details endpoint -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ready"
}

### Bad query parameters -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=shipped&limit=500

### Unknown route -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/nope
